@startuml m1-video-source-flow
title Video source lifecycle — from a clip on disk to R19 evidence

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

|User|
start
:Source one ego-POV clip: B ahead and occluding, C never visible in any frame;
:Re-encode: ffmpeg -c:v libx264 -vf scale=1280:720 -r 20 -an -movflags +faststart;
:Verify with ffprobe against the input spec, then commit it once to ADA_ECU/media/;

|CI / build|
:docker buildx build --platform linux/arm64 --provenance=false --sbom=false;
:COPY media/ is its own early layer, so an unchanged clip is never re-uploaded;
:docker push to registry.hackathon-2.carsky.io/m1-ada-ecu:latest;

|CarSky platform|
:Deploy the blueprint; the ADA node pulls the image;
:Deployment Viewer reports every node Running (R5);

|ADA ECU|
:Detector opens VIDEO_CLIP_PATH through the FrameSource seam (OpenCV VideoCapture);
:Sample every DETECTOR_FRAME_STRIDE-th frame — 5 Hz effective at stride 4;
:YOLO11n ONNX CPU inference; pinhole known-width distance for B;
:Emit R3 TrackedObject JSONL on stdout with source = own_sensor;
:Core admits B via R13, fuses relayed C from R2, emits R4 to the IVI (R15);

|IVI ECU|
:Render the R17 warning view — ego, B, ghost C — from R4 alone;
if (dashcam view accepted as additive, timeboxed scope?) then (yes)
  :Media3 plays the same clip from DASHCAM_MEDIA_URI behind the warning overlay;
  :Detector switches to real-time pacing so the picture and the warnings do not drift;
else (no — M1 committed scope)
  :Display area shows the warning view only;
endif

|Evidence|
:check_zero_c.py confirms zero entries labelled C across the whole detection log;
:pcap of ADA -> IVI UDP corroborates the R4 chain (R15, R19);
:One continuous recorded run closes R19;
stop

legend right
  <b>Legend — R-numbers are requirement IDs from the report §2, not a message namespace.</b>
  <b>R1–R6</b> are //contract// requirements (deliverable = a schema or a topology), so
  "an R3 object" or "the R4 warning" names the artifact that requirement defines.
  <b>R7–R19</b> are //behavioural// requirements (deliverable = running code).
  ====
  |= ID |= Kind |= Meaning on this flow |
  | R2 | contract | V2X ECU → ADA object message — the relayed C the core fuses in |
  | R3 | contract | <b>TrackedObject</b> schema — the JSONL shape the detector emits, `source = own_sensor` |
  | R4 | contract | ADA → IVI warning message the core sends and the IVI renders |
  | R5 | contract | node deployment — "every node Running" is R5's acceptance check |
  | R12 | behaviour | object detection from video — the whole detector lane |
  | R13 | behaviour | admission state machine that promotes B into a tracked object |
  | R15 | behaviour | the emitter of R4 — edge-triggered on a risk transition |
  | R17 | behaviour | the IVI warning view: ego, B, ghost C |
  | R19 | behaviour | definition of done — one continuous run, zero direct C detections |
  ====
  <b>ego / B / C.</b> ego = vehicle A, the warned car · B = the visible occluder ahead · C = the occluded
  car A can never see. <b>Zero-C check</b> = R19's evidence that C never appeared to A's own camera.
endlegend

@enduml
